<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36467" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pĭtănē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πιτάνη</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A city on the Æolic coast of Asia
			Minor</i>, now <i>Sandarlik</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 18,
				1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 7, 357</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pĭtănaeus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of Pitane</i>, <i>Pitanean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Apollonius Pitanaeus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					29, 6, 38, § 117</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A town in Laconia</i>, <i>on the
				Eurotas</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 5, 8, § 16</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Aus. Epigr. 24, 3</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
